{
    "background_story": "Sarai was a brilliant pharmacologist who had dedicated her career to developing new treatments for arthritis. She spent years researching and experimenting, driven by the memory of her grandmother who suffered from debilitating joint pain. Sarai's breakthrough came when she discovered a novel application for piroxicam, a nonsteroidal anti-inflammatory drug (NSAID). Her innovative approach led to the creation of a new medication that not only reduced inflammation but also promoted tissue repair. The medication, which Sarai dubbed 'Piroxa', quickly gained FDA approval and became a game-changer for millions of people worldwide. Sarai's work with piroxicam earned her numerous accolades, including the prestigious National Science Award. Her dedication to improving human health had left a lasting impact, and her name became synonymous with groundbreaking research.",
